DATA SOURCES AND ATTRIBUTION

This benchmark is built entirely from publicly available data sources.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GitHub Security Advisory Database
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This benchmark uses vulnerability metadata from the GitHub Security Advisory
Database (https://github.com/advisories), including:

  - Vulnerability descriptions (GHSA entries)
  - Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVE) identifiers
  - Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE) classifications
  - Severity ratings and CVSS scores

The GitHub Security Advisory Database is publicly accessible and subject to
GitHub's Terms of Service (https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy).

We gratefully acknowledge the security researchers who discovered and
responsibly disclosed these vulnerabilities, and the GitHub team for
maintaining this public resource.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Open Source Repository Snapshots
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This benchmark requires snapshots of open source repositories at specific
commits (both vulnerable and patched states). It provides a utility to fetch
the dataset repository content. Each repository retains its
original open source license.

IMPORTANT: All repository content is subject to the original repository's
license terms. The complete license information for each of the 500 included
repositories is documented in data/manifest.csv (columns: vulnerable_LICENSE
and merge_LICENSE).

License Distribution of Included Repositories:
  - Apache-2.0:    241 repositories (48.2%)
  - MIT:           161 repositories (32.2%)
  - Other:          46 repositories (9.2%)
  - GPL-3.0:        15 repositories (3.0%)
  - LGPL:           12 repositories (2.4%)
  - MPL-2.0:        12 repositories (2.4%)
  - BSD-3-Clause:    5 repositories (1.0%)
  - Creative Commons: 4 repositories (0.8%)
  - ISC:             2 repositories (0.4%)
  - GPL-2.0:         1 repository  (0.2%)
  - AGPL-3.0:        1 repository  (0.2%)

We acknowledge and thank all open source maintainers whose repositories are
included in this benchmark. Their contributions to open source software and
responsible vulnerability disclosure make this research possible.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
License Compliance Requirements
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Users of this benchmark MUST:

1. Comply with the license terms of each included repository
2. Retain all copyright notices and license information from original repositories
3. Refer to data/manifest.csv for specific license information per repository
4. Acknowledge that repository snapshots are provided for research and
   evaluation purposes

No modifications were made to any repository licenses between vulnerable and
patched states.

================================================================================

DISCLAIMER

This benchmark provides historical snapshots of vulnerabilities for research
and evaluation purposes. The vulnerability information and code snapshots
reflect the state at the time of dataset creation and may not represent
current repository states.

THE BENCHMARK IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
